<div class="ds-prose">
  <p>Last updated: {{ last_updated | formatDate }}</p>

  <p>
    Guido is designed to work entirely on your device and your local network. It does not create an account, does not
    require you to sign in, and does not send any of your data to our servers.
  </p>

  <h2>Information We Collect</h2>

  <p>We do not collect, store, or transmit any personal information.</p>

  <h2>Telemetry Data</h2>

  <p>
    Guido receives live telemetry from your simulator (Gran Turismo 7 or Assetto Corsa Competizione) over your local
    network and displays it on screen. This data never leaves your local network and is not stored or transmitted by the
    app.
  </p>

  <h2>Microphone</h2>

  <p>
    Guido may access your microphone (with your permission) to support push-to-talk voice commands and, where enabled,
    hands-free wake-word listening. Audio is captured only while you are actively using a voice feature and is processed
    on-device by a speech recognition model that ships with the app. It is not recorded, stored, or transmitted
    anywhere.
  </p>

  <h2>Local Storage</h2>

  <p>
    Guido stores a small set of preferences on your device — such as your preferred speed and temperature units, a
    manually entered simulator address, and the last simulator used. This information stays on your device and is only
    used to personalize the app. You can clear it by uninstalling the app or clearing its app data.
  </p>

  <h2>Permissions</h2>

  <p>
    Guido uses the following permissions, solely for the features described above:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Internet / network state</strong> — to receive telemetry from your simulator over the local network.</li>
    <li><strong>Microphone</strong> — for on-device voice commands.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>

  <p>
    Guido contains no third-party advertising, analytics, crash reporting, or tracking SDKs. The app is distributed
    through the Google Play Store; Google may collect information about installations and updates in accordance with
    Google's own privacy policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>

  <p>If you have questions about this privacy policy, please <a href="/contact/">contact us</a>.</p>
</div>